        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Leftovers", "{DL} says they were left over from an earlier event."), E(.statement, 1, "Resale", "{DL} says {D.he} thought resale was allowed.")],
        role: "Fair gate manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did your gate scanner show?", "\"Eleven wristbands rejected in an hour. All eleven had the same serial number.\""), .direct("How were they identified?", "\"They were color copies. Staff traced them to a seller in a gray cap who matched {D}.\""), .direct("What was found in {D}'s van?", "\"Blank wristband stock and a laminator. That is the kind of equipment used to make copies.\""), .direct("How do your wristbands normally work at the fair?", "\"Each is a numbered paper band with a unique serial number and a security thread. The gate scanner reads the number and flags any duplicate.\""), .direct("What happened at the gate that day?", "\"Within an hour the scanner rejected eleven bands with the same serial number. I pulled a few aside and saw they were color copies without the security thread.\""), .direct("How did your staff trace the copies?", "\"Families told us they bought them in the parking field for $15 from someone in a gray cap. A staff member spotted the seller and called me.\""), .cross("{D} says the wristbands were left over from an earlier event, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D} says so. But the serial number on each was the same, which leftovers would not be.\""), .cross("Did {D} sell only to families on foot?", "\"I understand so. {D} did not stand in the road.\""), .cross("Did {D} charge less than the gate?", "\"Yes. $15 each, which was below the gate price.\""), .cross("Are blank wristband stock and a laminator evidence of copying?", "\"They are consistent with it. They are also items an event vendor might have for ordinary reasons.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} print the wristbands?", "\"No. We have no witness to the printing. We have the copies, the scanner, and what was in the van.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold copied wristbands to fairgoers.", "A seller reselling leftover wristbands."),
