        defendant: [.direct("Did you make the wristband copies?", "\"No. I did not make them. They were leftovers from an earlier event, and I resold them.\""), .direct("Why did you charge $15?", "\"It was a discount. I thought families would like a deal, and I priced it below the gate.\""), .direct("What about the laminator in your van?", "\"I use it for work. I laminate signs and flyers. It had nothing to do with wristbands.\""), .direct("Where did you get the stock in your van?", "\"From an earlier event where I worked as a vendor. We had leftover bands and a few rolls of blank stock that I kept.\""), .direct("Why did you sell in the parking field?", "\"Families were walking in and asked about discounts. I figured selling leftovers cheaply was a way to move them.\""), .direct("How did you set the price?", "\"I picked $15 because it seemed fair compared to the gate price. I did not think about the fair losing revenue.\""), .cross("Every wristband you sold had the same serial number. How is that possible?", "\"I did not look at the numbers. I assumed they were valid.\""), .cross("Blank wristband stock was in your van, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was leftover stock. I did not use it to print copies.\""), .cross("The gate manager identified you by your gray cap, didn't the manager?", "\"Yes. It is my cap. I do not deny I was selling.\""), .cross("Eleven bands with the same serial number is not a mistake. Who made them?", "\"I did not. I assumed the leftovers each had their own number. I did not read the serials.\""), .cross("You carry a laminator in your van. Why?", "\"For signs and flyers. I laminate a lot of paper for work, and the machine is part of my kit.\"")],
