        summary: "A bowling alley's manager gave {D} a written trespass notice after a fight at the snack bar. Six weeks later, on {DATE}, {D} walked in wearing a team shirt and started warming up on lane 12 for league night. The manager recognized {D} and asked {D.him} to leave twice. {D} stayed through two frames until deputies arrived. {DL} says the league secretary told {D.him} the ban did not apply to league play.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Trespass Notice", "Signed by {D} six weeks earlier."), E(.video, 2, "Lane Camera", "{D} bowls on lane 12 after being asked to leave."), E(.document, 2, "League Roster", "{D}'s name added after the ban."), E(.statement, 1, "Manager", "Asked {D} to leave twice.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Secretary's Word", "{DL} says the league secretary said it was fine."), E(.statement, 1, "Team Jersey", "{DL} says {D.his} team needed a fourth bowler.")],
        role: "Bowling alley manager",
        exam: [.direct("What notice did you give {DL}?", "\"A written trespass notice after a fight at our snack bar. {D} signed it, six weeks before {DATE}.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"{D} walked in wearing a team shirt and began warming up on lane 12 for league night. I recognized {D} and asked {D.him} to leave twice.\""), .direct("What happened after you asked?", "\"{D} stayed and bowled two frames until deputies arrived. The lane camera shows it.\""), .direct("What led to the trespass notice?", "\"A fight broke out at the snack bar about six weeks earlier. I told {D} to leave and had {D} sign a written notice banning {D} from the property.\""), .direct("How did you spot {D} on league night?", "\"I was working the front desk and saw {D} walk in wearing a team shirt. {D} headed straight for lane 12 and began warming up.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I walked over and told {D} that the notice was still in effect and to leave. I asked a second time a few minutes later.\""), .cross("{DL} says the league secretary said the ban did not apply to league play, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The league secretary doesn't set my trespass policy. I own the decision.\""), .cross("Was {DL}'s name on the league roster?", "\"Yes, added after the ban. That means someone put it there. I don't know who.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cause trouble that night?", "\"No. {D} bowled and stayed calm. The only issue was staying after I asked.\""), .cross("Did {D} threaten you or the other bowlers?", "\"No. {D} was calm and said the league secretary had cleared it.\""), .cross("Who put {D}'s name on the league roster?", "\"I do not know. The league secretary manages that list, and I did not approve it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} came back after a written ban.", "A bowler told the ban did not cover league play."),
        allocution: "\"I understand why people were afraid. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had signed the notice and kept a copy in {D.his} bowling bag.", "{DL} entered through the staff side door."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you come to league night?", "\"My team needed a fourth bowler. The league secretary told me the ban did not apply to league play.\""), .direct("Did you know about the notice?", "\"I knew I'd signed one after the fight. But I thought league play was different, because the secretary said so.\""), .direct("Why did you stay after being asked?", "\"I thought the secretary was right. I wanted to finish my frames. I didn't mean to defy anyone.\""), .direct("How long have you bowled in the league?", "\"Six years. I bowl on Thursdays with the same team, and we know most of the players.\""), .direct("Why did you come back after the ban?", "\"Our team was a bowler short and risked forfeiting. The league secretary said the ban was for open play and league night was different.\""), .direct("Where did you keep the notice?", "\"I stuffed a copy in my bowling bag and forgot about it. I should have read it again.\""), .cross("You signed the notice, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I signed it. I knew about it.\""), .cross("The manager asked you twice to leave, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes. And I stayed two frames. I should have left.\""), .cross("The secretary doesn't own the alley, does the secretary?", "\"No. I know that. I should have asked the manager first.\""), .cross("The notice named the whole property. Why believe a league secretary over a written notice?", "\"Because the secretary seemed to know the rules. I should have called the manager.\""), .cross("You were asked twice to leave. Why bowl two more frames?", "\"I wanted to finish out the frame and thought I had permission. I know that was a mistake.\"")],
        openings: ("After a snack bar fight, a bowling alley manager gave {D} a written trespass notice. Six weeks later, {D} walked in for league night, was asked twice to leave, and stayed two frames until deputies arrived. The State will show the notice, the lane camera, and the roster.", "The defense will point you to a bowler who was told by the league secretary that the ban did not apply to league play, and who joined a team that needed a fourth."),
        closings: ("A signed trespass notice, a return six weeks later, two requests to leave, and two more frames. {D} knew the ban and stayed anyway.", "The league secretary said the ban did not apply to league play, and {D} believed it. The State has not proved {D} knowingly trespassed."),
        timeline: [(-42, "The fight and the notice."), (-3, "{D} is added to the league roster."), (0, "7 p.m.: {D} enters by the side door."), (0, "7:20 p.m.: the manager asks {D} to leave."), (0, "7:40 p.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "A trespass notice.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let benchSmashV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.benchSmash",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Bus Shelter Glass Panel Shattered by Skateboard, Repair Estimate $700", "Transit Camera Shows Rider Run Board Into the Panel on Purpose"],
        law: "injuryRealProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured real property of {V}, a city, causing damage of $700, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A city transit shelter's glass panel was shattered on {DATE}. A transit camera showed {D} take a skateboard, back up and strike the panel with the board's edge twice. The city's repair estimate was $700. Security found the board with chipped glass fragments in a trash can nearby. {DL} says it was an accident and that the board slipped while {D.he} did a trick.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Transit Camera", "{D} swings the board into the panel twice."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimate", "$700 to replace the panel."), E(.physical, 2, "Skateboard", "Glass fragments in the edge of the board."), E(.statement, 1, "Bus Driver", "Saw {D} at the shelter.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Accident", "{DL} says the board slipped on a trick."), E(.statement, 1, "Dare", "{DL} says friends dared {D.him} to jump the curb.")],
        role: "City transit supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to the transit shelter on {DATE}?", "\"A glass panel was shattered. The city's repair estimate is $700 to replace it.\""), .direct("What does the transit camera show?", "\"{D} taking a skateboard, backing up, and striking the panel twice with the edge of the board.\""), .direct("What did security find?", "\"The board in a trash can nearby, with chipped glass fragments in the edge. It ties the board to the panel.\""), .direct("How did the damage come to your office's attention?", "\"A bus driver called in a shattered panel at a stop. We sent a crew and pulled the shelter camera footage the same afternoon.\""), .direct("How was the panel replaced and what did it cost?", "\"Tempered glass, cut to size, and installed by a contractor. The estimate was $700, and the shelter was closed for two days.\""), .direct("What did security find near the shelter?", "\"A skateboard in a trash can a few yards away with fine glass chips lodged in the edge. They bagged it and logged it.\""), .cross("{DL} says it was an accident, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"The camera shows two strikes, not one. A slip would not usually happen twice.\""), .cross("Did a bus driver see {DL}?", "\"Yes. The driver saw {D} at the shelter. The driver didn't see the strikes.\""), .cross("Was anyone hurt?", "\"No. The shelter was empty. It could have injured someone, though.\""), .cross("Did anyone see {D} intend to break the panel?", "\"The footage shows two strikes. Whether {D} intended it is for the jury, not for me.\""), .cross("Was the shelter in use at the time?", "\"No. No one was inside. The panel could have caused injury if someone had been there.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shattered a shelter panel on purpose.", "A skater whose board slipped."),
        allocution: "\"I wasn't thinking about the person on the other end. I am now.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} laughed after the second strike.", "{DL} threw the board into a trash can before leaving."),
        defendant: [.direct("What were you doing at the shelter?", "\"Skating with friends. We were doing tricks, and my board slipped and hit the glass.\""), .direct("Why does the camera show two strikes?", "\"The board slipped on a trick and I tried again. My friends had dared me to jump the curb.\""), .direct("Did you mean to break the panel?", "\"No. It was an accident. I'd never break a shelter on purpose.\""), .direct("Who were you with at the shelter?", "\"A couple of friends. We were skating the curb, trying kickflips and board-slides.\""), .direct("What exactly was the trick you tried?", "\"A jump off the curb into a board slide. I backed up to get speed, and the board shot out sideways and hit the glass.\""), .direct("What did you do after it broke?", "\"I panicked and laughed because I did not know what else to do. I tossed the board in a trash can and left.\""), .cross("The camera shows you backing up, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. That was the trick. I needed room to jump.\""), .cross("You hit it twice, didn't you?", "\"The board hit twice. It happened fast. I didn't realize at first.\""), .cross("Glass was in the edge of your board, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. That's from the hit. I'm so sorry.\""), .cross("The camera shows two strikes. Why would a slip hit twice?", "\"I tried the trick again after the first slip. I did not mean to hit the glass.\""), .cross("Why throw the board in the trash?", "\"I was scared. I did not want to be caught with it. I know how that looks.\"")],
        openings: ("A city transit shelter's glass panel was shattered, and the transit camera shows {D} take a skateboard, back up, and strike the panel twice with its edge. The $700 repair is in evidence. The State will show the video and the board.", "The defense will present a skater doing a trick on a dare, a board that slipped, and a person who stayed and did not hide."),
        closings: ("Two strikes on camera, glass chips in the edge of {D}'s board, and a skateboard thrown in a trash can as {D} walked off. A slip does not hit twice, and it does not hide the evidence.", "A trick that went wrong on a dare, a board that slipped on a curb, and a skater who panicked afterward. The State has not proved {D} meant to break the glass rather than land a trick."),
        timeline: [(0, "4:10 p.m.: {D} arrives with friends."), (0, "4:14 p.m.: the first strike."), (0, "4:15 p.m.: the second strike."), (0, "4:30 p.m.: security finds the board."), (1, "The city gets a repair estimate.")],
        identified: "A transit camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let utilityGiftCardsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.utilityGiftCards",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Restaurant Owner Pays $900 in Gift Cards After Gas Bill Call", "Caller Says Kitchen Gas Will Be Cut in an Hour"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        spec: "Obtained property of {V}, a restaurant owner, by deception, $900, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} got a call at 10:30 a.m. on {DATE} from a person claiming to be the gas company who said the restaurant's service would be cut in an hour unless an overdue bill was paid in gift cards. {V} bought $900 in cards at a drugstore by 11:20 a.m. and read the codes over the phone. The cards were spent that afternoon. The calling number belongs to {D}'s prepaid line.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Call Records", "Two calls to the restaurant from a prepaid line registered to {D} at 10:30 and 10:58 a.m."), E(.document, 3, "Card Receipts", "Nine $100 cards bought at a drugstore between 11:05 and 11:20 a.m."), E(.digital, 2, "Redemption Log", "The cards were redeemed within an hour to an account in {D}'s name."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "The caller used the real gas company name and a phone number that looked local.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Phone Taken", "{DL} says the prepaid line was lent to a friend that week."), E(.statement, 1, "Account Shared", "{DL} says the redemption account was used by a roommate.")],
        role: "Restaurant owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did the caller tell you?", "\"That I was from the gas company's overdue accounts and service would be cut in an hour unless I paid in gift cards.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I bought $900 in gift cards at a drugstore by 11:20 a.m. and read the codes over the phone.\""), .direct("How was the caller traced?", "\"The calling number belongs to a prepaid line registered to {D}. The redemption log shows the cards redeemed to an account in {D}'s name.\""), .direct("What was the first call like?", "\"The caller said I owed an overdue gas bill and service would be shut off in an hour unless I paid right away with gift cards. The voice was calm and firm.\""), .direct("What did you do after the second call?", "\"I went to a drugstore and bought nine $100 cards. I called back and read the numbers over the phone at about 11:20.\""), .direct("What happened to the money?", "\"The cards were spent that afternoon. The gas company later told me I never owed a bill.\""), .cross("A roommate shared that prepaid line, didn't one?", "\"I heard that. I do not know who used the phone.\""), .cross("Did you hear the caller's voice?", "\"Yes. I cannot say it was {D}'s. It was a stranger's voice.\""), .cross("The caller used the real gas company name, didn't the caller?", "\"Yes. That is part of why I believed it.\""), .cross("Did you check the number the caller gave?", "\"I looked at the caller ID and it showed a local-looking number. I did not call the gas company directly.\""), .cross("Do you know whose phone it was?", "\"Only what deputies told me, that it was a prepaid line registered to {D}.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Former roommate",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you share a phone or account with {D}?", "\"A prepaid line and the same account for a few months, back when we lived together.\""), .direct("When did you move out?", "\"In the spring. I had already left by the time those calls were made that week.\""), .direct("Did you ever use the prepaid line yourself?", "\"Sometimes, for deliveries. I used it for work, and I did not keep track of who else used it.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"I lived with {D} for about a year. We shared the apartment, the Wi-Fi, and a prepaid phone.\""), .direct("Who used the prepaid line?", "\"Whoever grabbed it. We left it on the kitchen counter and used it for calls when our own phones were dead.\""), .direct("Did you ever use the account in {D}'s name?", "\"Yes, sometimes. We kept the login in a note on the fridge, and I used it for small transactions.\""), .cross("Did you make any calls to restaurants that week?", "\"No. I was not there that week. I was out of town, and I did not call anyone.\""), .cross("Do you know who used the phone after you left?", "\"No. {D} kept the line after I moved out. I do not know who else used it.\""), .cross("Are you still in touch with {D}?", "\"Not much. We lost touch after I moved out.\""), .cross("Were you in the apartment the week of the calls?", "\"I moved out in the spring, so I was gone. I am telling you who had the phone and the login while I lived there.\""), .cross("Did you ever hear {D} call restaurants?", "\"No. I never heard anything like that.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ran a gift card scam on a restaurant.", "The phone and the account were lent to others."),
        allocution: "\"I took advantage of someone who trusted me, and I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had called twelve other restaurants that week.", "A roommate shared the prepaid phone and the account."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you call the restaurant?", "\"No. I did not call it. I do not know that restaurant.\""), .direct("Whose phone was it?", "\"A prepaid line that a former roommate and I shared. The roommate used it too.\""), .direct("What about the gift cards redeemed to your account?", "\"The account was shared with the roommate. I did not redeem those cards myself.\""), .direct("How long did you have the prepaid line?", "\"A few months. I used it for a side job and shared it with a roommate for deliveries.\""), .direct("Who else used the line?", "\"My roommate. We split the account and passed the phone back and forth.\""), .direct("Where were you on the morning of the calls?", "\"At work, on a shift that started at eight. I could not have called a restaurant at 10:30.\""), .cross("The calling number is registered to you, isn't it?", "\"Yes. But the line was shared, and I did not make those calls.\""), .cross("The cards were redeemed to an account in your name within an hour, weren't they?", "\"The account is in my name, but a roommate had access. I did not redeem them.\""), .cross("Twelve other restaurants got calls that week. How do you explain that?", "\"I do not. I was not the caller.\""), .cross("The cards were redeemed to an account in your name. Who has access?", "\"My roommate used it too. I did not redeem the cards.\""), .cross("Twelve other restaurants got calls that week from the same line. Doesn't that show a pattern?", "\"It shows someone using the line a lot. It was not me.\"")],
        openings: ("A caller posing as the gas company told a restaurant owner that service would be cut in an hour unless an overdue bill was paid in gift cards. The owner bought $900 in cards, and the call came from a prepaid line registered to {D}.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that the prepaid line and account were shared with a roommate, who used them, and that {D} made no such calls."),
        closings: ("Two calls from {D}'s registered line, nine $100 cards bought and read over the phone, and the cards redeemed to {D}'s account within the hour. Twelve other restaurants got calls too.", "A shared prepaid phone, a shared account, and a roommate with access. The State has the line and the account, but not the caller's voice."),
        timeline: [(0, "10:30 a.m.: the first call to the restaurant."), (0, "11:20 a.m.: the last gift card is bought."), (0, "12:30 p.m.: the cards are redeemed."), (2, "{V} learns from the gas company that no bill was overdue.")],
        identified: "A prepaid line and a redemption account in {D}'s name led to {D}.",
        notDone: ["The former roommate who moved out was never located.", "No one asked who was using the prepaid line that morning."],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let payrollCheckCashV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.payrollCheckCash",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Mailed Tax Refund Check Cashed at Grocery Store Counter With a Scanned ID, Victim Never Got the Envelope", "Mail Theft Report Filed the Same Day the Check Was Cashed"],
        law: "uttering",
        spec: "Uttered a forged check to {V}, a check-cashing store, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A homeowner reported on {DATE} that a state tax refund check never arrived in the mail. The same day a grocery store's check-cashing counter paid $620 on that check. The endorsement was a forgery. The counter scanned the ID of the person who cashed it, and the ID belonged to {D}. {DL} says {D.he} was handed the check by a friend as repayment of a debt and did not know it was stolen.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Check", "A forged endorsement on a $620 refund check."), E(.document, 2, "ID Scan", "{D}'s license scanned at the counter."), E(.document, 2, "Mail Theft Report", "Filed the same day the check was cashed."), E(.video, 1, "Counter Camera", "{D} at the counter.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Friend's Repayment", "{DL} says a friend gave {D.him} the check."), E(.statement, 1, "Didn't Know", "{DL} says {D.he} thought it was valid.")],
        role: "Check-cashing clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What came across your counter that day?", "\"A $620 state tax refund check. The person cashing it scanned an ID that belonged to {D}.\""), .direct("What was wrong with the check?", "\"The endorsement was a forgery. The homeowner reported the check stolen from the mail the same day.\""), .direct("What does the counter camera show?", "\"{D} at the counter. The ID scan and the camera line up.\""), .direct("What did the person present at your counter?", "\"A $620 state tax refund check made out to someone else, with an endorsement signature on the back and a driver's license.\""), .direct("How does your counter verify a check?", "\"We scan the ID, compare the face to the camera, check the endorsement, and verify the amount against our limits. {D}'s ID passed the scanner.\""), .direct("How did the forgery come to light?", "\"The homeowner reported the refund missing from the mail the same day. A week later the state flagged the check as altered.\""), .cross("{D} says a friend handed over the check as repayment, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D} says so, and {D} used a real ID. That is accurate.\""), .cross("Did {D} ask another clerk a question first?", "\"Yes. I heard {D} asked whether a check could be cashed 'without the owner.' That bothered me.\""), .cross("Could {D} name the friend?", "\"No. {D} could not name the friend.\""), .cross("Did {D} seem nervous at the counter?", "\"No. {D} was calm and answered my questions. I noticed nothing unusual about how {D} behaved.\""), .cross("Why did you cash a check made out to another person?", "\"Third-party checks are allowed with an endorsement. The signature looked plausible to me, and the ID matched the person at the window.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cashed a stolen refund check with a forged endorsement.", "A person repaid with a bad check."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry to everyone I let down. I'll repay what I can.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had asked another clerk whether a check could be cashed 'without the owner'.", "{DL} could not name the friend."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cash that check?", "\"Yes, I did. A friend handed it to me as repayment of a debt, and I did not know it was stolen.\""), .direct("Why did you use your real ID?", "\"I had nothing to hide. I thought it was an ordinary check, and I used my own license.\""), .direct("Who gave you the check?", "\"A friend. I know the first name only. I do not have a way to reach the friend now.\""), .direct("How did you come to have the check?", "\"A friend owed me money and handed me the check one evening. I was told it was part of a refund and that the friend would sign it over.\""), .direct("What did you do with it?", "\"I took it to the counter the next day and used my own license. I did not think of hiding who I was.\""), .direct("What did you do with the cash?", "\"I paid some bills and kept the rest. I did not know it was stolen.\""), .cross("The endorsement was forged, wasn't it?", "\"I did not sign it. The friend must have. I did not look closely.\""), .cross("You cannot name the friend. Why should we believe you?", "\"I know. I wish I could. All I can say is that I thought it was repayment.\""), .cross("Why would a friend repay a debt with a stranger's tax refund?", "\"I did not think it through. I assumed the friend had signed it over, and I should have asked more.\""), .cross("You asked a clerk whether a check could be cashed 'without the owner.' Why?", "\"I was curious about whether a third party could cash it. I did not know it was stolen.\""), .cross("You never asked the friend for a phone number or a last name, did you?", "\"No. I trusted the friend and never asked. I know that sounds careless, and I have not been able to reach the friend since.\"")],
        openings: ("A homeowner's $620 state tax refund check was stolen from the mail and cashed the same day at a grocery check counter. The endorsement was forged, and the ID scanned at the counter belongs to {D}.", "The defense case is that a friend handed {D} the check as repayment of a debt, that {D} used a real ID, and that {D} did not know it was stolen."),
        closings: ("A stolen refund check, a forged endorsement, {D}'s ID at the counter, and a question about cashing a check 'without the owner.' {D} took the cash.", "{D} used a real ID, hid nothing, and believed a friend's repayment was good. The State must prove {D} knew the check was stolen."),
        timeline: [(-3, "The refund is mailed."), (-1, "The envelope is stolen."), (0, "{D} cashes the check."), (0, "The homeowner reports it missing."), (1, "The scan is pulled.")],
        identified: "A check and an ID scan.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])
}
